      "claim": "Fed-state evidence remains above threshold: KNI-272 capsule post-prandial F=36.40% (6.6 mg/kg) and 22.06% (4 mg/kg), and food increased propranolol F from 0.27 to 0.46, so fed administration does not provide affirmative evidence for low F.",
      "card_ids": ["C09", "C50", "C67"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Etodolac, an ionizable carboxylic acid, has reported absolute bioavailability of 0.80 from the FDA approval package and estimates near 1, with >80% in normal adults, demonstrating that acidic molecules can achieve high oral F.",
      "card_ids": ["C17", "C20", "C05", "C41"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Sub-20% L2 records are non-human or formulation-specific (propranolol dog 15.6%, S-propranolol rat 12±9%, FK788 rat 9.6%, KNI-272 cherry syrup fed 15.72%) and do not constitute affirmative human-relevant evidence for F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C28", "C54", "C45", "C29"]
    }
  ],
