      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C29", "C45", "C28", "C54"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "No fed-state pharmacokinetic study is available for the query; the fed effect is inferred only from other molecules.",
    "No experimental permeability or solubility data are available for the query; the logD-based prior is indirect.",
    "FK788 and etodolac are structurally related but not identical to the query, with differences in logD, molecular weight, and metabolic clearance.",
    "Sub-20% L2 values come from non-human species or alternative formulations (cherry syrup), limiting their transferability to a human oral solid-dose fed-state prediction."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F≥20%) because all human L1 records are ≥20%, including aryloxyacetic acid FK788 (55%), ionizable carboxylic acid etodolac (80–100%), and fed-state KNI-272 capsule (36.4%); new L2 evidence adds fed-state support (food raised propranolol F from 0.27 to 0.46; KNI-272 fed capsule 22.06%) while sub-20% L2 records are non-human or formulation-specific and do not affirmatively support F<20%."
}

